rows=[
('prepare','Prepare the warm bike','Begin with the assembled stock bike at operating temperature, engine stopped, on level ground. Wear gloves and clothing suitable for hot oil. Place a drain container below the engine and arrange secure support for later side positioning. Identify the drain plug, screen plugs and filter cover before opening anything.',[134],False,True),
('drain','Drain the oil','Remove magnetic drain plug 1 and its seal ring. Remove screen plug 2 and its O-ring. Leave the lower adjacent screw A in place. Remove plug 3, long screen 4 and the O-rings. Let the oil finish draining, then thoroughly clean the removed parts and their sealing surfaces.',[134],False,True),
('plug-two','Refit the first screen plug','Refit plug 2 with its O-ring and tighten the M20 x 1.5 plug to 15 Nm. The adjacent screw A stays untouched.',[134,135],True,True),
('screen','Seat the long screen','Place the long screen and its O-rings on a pin wrench. Position the pin wrench through the drill hole of the screw plug on the opposite section of the engine case as illustrated and push the screen fully into the case. Confirm seating before fitting its plug.',[135],False,True),
('plugs','Close the drain openings','Fit screen plug 3 with its O-ring and tighten to 15 Nm. Fit the magnetic drain plug with a NEW seal ring and tighten its M12 x 1.5 thread to 20 Nm. Record both torque settings.',[135],True,True),
('filter-out','Remove the used filter','Remove the two cover screws identified by callout 5 and lift away the cover and O-ring. Use lock ring pliers 51012011000 to withdraw the filter. Let the remaining oil drain and clean the parts and sealing surfaces.',[135],False,True),
('filter-in','Prime and fit the new filter','Lay the bike on its side with the filter opening upward as shown. Fill the housing about one-third with fresh engine oil, then insert the new filter. Lubricate the cover O-ring and fit it with the cover. Tighten both M6 x 16 cover screws to 10 Nm.',[136],True,True),
('fill','Refill the engine','Return the bike upright. Remove the filler plug and O-ring and refill with fully synthetic 10W/50 engine oil. The specified service quantity is 1.20 L; record the oil and amount used and confirm the result with the final level check. Refit and tighten the filler plug with its O-ring.',[136],True,True),
('run','Start and check for leaks','With oil and all closures installed, remove the plug-in stand, support the bike and select neutral. Use a well-ventilated area or suitable exhaust extraction indoors. Below 20 C ambient, press the cold-start button fully in. Limit each starter attempt to 5 seconds; wait 15 seconds between attempts, or 30 seconds at low temperatures. Stop after six failed attempts and investigate. Warm a cold engine only at low speed. If the cold-start button was used, turn the throttle grip forward to return it. Inspect oil plugs and filter cover for leaks. Stop for leaks or abnormal noise; switch off if idling or stationary running is likely to last one minute or longer.',[32,33,36,136],False,False),
('level','Measure the oil level','Stop the idling engine with the stop button. Hold the bike upright on level ground. At operating temperature, wait one minute after stopping: the level must lie between the middle and upper edge of the sight glass. For a fully cold check, the target is the middle. Record temperature condition and actual level. Below-middle needs topping up; an above-target or unreadable result needs correction or investigation before completion.',[38,133],True,True),
('topup','Correct a low level if needed','If the target is already met, record no top-up needed. Otherwise stop the engine, remove the filler plug and O-ring and add the same oil used for this change, only as needed for the specified level. Do not add another 1.20 L as a top-up dose or mix oil types. Refit the plug and O-ring; repeat the preceding start/leak check, then stop and check the level for the actual temperature condition. Record any oil added and the accepted final level. An unresolved result does not complete this job.',[133,137],True,False),
('finish','Save the service','Confirm the engine is stopped, the final level is accepted and no leak remains. Save oil, quantity, completed plug/cover torques and level result. Dispose of the drained oil and used filter through an appropriate waste facility.',[134,135,136,137],False,False)
]
